WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.570
My name is Chengkai Zhang.

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:03.660
And the project that
I have been working on

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.780
is the learning of
3D-shaped priors

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:09.340
that can be used to help
with other 3D tasks.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.400
So what is a shape prior?

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.920
Basically, it's the sense of
what a shape should look like.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.820
So for example, if I
take two random chairs

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.270
of different styles and then
I put the back of one chair

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.760
on the seat of the
other one, then

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.370
I will end up getting a shape
that can be defined as a chair,

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:29.430
but probably you'll say
that this chair looks weird,

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:30.730
it doesn't look right.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.880
So this is because we've built
a sense of what a chair should

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:37.530
look like over years of seeing
different kinds of chairs.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.500
So right now, we try to build
a neural network that models

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.120
this kind of knowledge.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.510
So from a model pod
we train a generator

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:48.030
over several networks.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:50.430
So these are two
networks, one of which

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:52.890
we call a generator
that tries to generate

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:56.460
a shape that looks like the
shape in a given data set.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:59.340
And then the discriminator
tries to distinguish

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:02.110
between the generated
shape and the real shape.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:04.209
So these two compete
against each other.

00:01:04.209 --> 00:01:06.390
And when the training
converge, the generator

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:08.310
will be able to
sample new shapes that

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:11.160
looks like real shapes,
that looks reasonable.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.290
And the discriminator
will be able to tell

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:14.820
if the shape looks natural.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.300
So then we can use this
network to help with our tasks,

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.150
like 3D shape
reconstruction, so that we

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:24.120
can make the reconstructed
shapes also have more details

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.240
and looks more natural.

